        "content": "<p>I'm learning about iterators.  I defined an instance of <code>Iterator</code> with one parameter.  I started a tactic proof for its finiteness.</p>\n<p>I'm stuck because I reach the point in unfolding where my own instance is mentioned, but then I don't know how to tell <code>rw</code> to use my definition of <code>IsPlausibleStep</code>.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">wff</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">WFF</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">Iterators</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Finite</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Position</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">wff</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Id</span>\n<span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">constructor</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">position</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">constructor</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">position'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- ⟨ w, h ⟩</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">IterM</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">IsPlausibleSuccessorOf</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">IterM</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">IsPlausibleStep</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">Iterator</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">IsPlausibleStep</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">step</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h₁</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">wff</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">instIteratorPosition</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">1</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">internalState</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">position</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">step</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h₂</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">⟩</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I get the error</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Invalid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rewrite</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">argument</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Expected</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">an</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">equality</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">or</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">iff</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">proof</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">or</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">definition</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">name</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">but</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">Iterator</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">IsPlausibleStep</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">internalState</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">position</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">step</span>\n<span class=\"n\">is</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">value</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">of</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Meanwhile I looked in the core to see how <code>ArrayIter</code>'s finiteness is proved.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">instance</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ArrayIterator</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">instFinite</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Pure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finite</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ArrayIterator</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Finite</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">of_finitenessRelation</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ArrayIterator</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">instFinitenessRelation</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>That led me to <code>FinitenessRelation</code> which I will study later.</p>\n<p>I sort of get it, that a complete proof of any iterator's finiteness would begin with boilerplate steps very like what I wrote, so I should learn to use <code>FinitenessRelation</code> instead.</p>\n<p>Still, please instruct me, what technicality is impeding my tactic proof.</p>",
